  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "# Request\nFull body tracking currently allows us to track the hip or foot bones of our avatar.\n\nI'd like the ability to track my avatar's chest instead, because it has no (visible) hips or feet.\n\n# Example\n- I have a humanoid avatar which utilizes no bones below the chest. It has a head, arms and a chest, but no hip or legs. \n- I'd love to use full body tracking to track my avatar's chest, but currently there's no proper way of doing that.\n- At the moment I'd have to track the (invisible) hip, which leads to VRChat's IK guessing where my chest is, instead of directly tracking my chest.\n\nCheers! ❤",
